init.description:
**Cloud** works out of the box and is right for almost everyone.

The two **local** modes are advanced. They keep Home Assistant in control of the thermostat when your internet is down, but **they only work after you add a DNS record on your router or DNS server** (Pi-hole, AdGuard Home, UniFi and others). If you aren't sure what that means, keep Cloud.

You can switch modes at any time; your devices, entities and history stay the same. When leaving a local mode for Cloud, delete the DNS record and power-cycle the thermostat. Guide: {docs_url}
